= Close the Institute of Memory

SLD's programme did not ask merely for a new director. It demanded dissolution
of the Institute of National Remembrance. Veterans say a left party should not
finance an official prosecutor of history; lawyers ask where the archives go.

- @sld_ipn_close
- @sld_ipn_archive
- @sld_ipn_refuse

@sld_ipn_close
title: Abolish the IPN and divide its functions
subtitle: A defining break with memory politics; SLD rallies while institutional conflict surges.
on-arrival: barons_strength += 5; barons_dissent -= 9; pzpr_history_concessions -= 3; pensioner_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; institutional_trust -= 3; public_trust -= 2; ko_relation -= 5; p2050_relation -= 5; psl_relation -= 4; government_coalition_dissent += 4; early_election_risk += 2; news_headline = "SLD demands abolition of the Institute of National Remembrance"

State archives move to a civilian archive, prosecutions to ordinary offices
and education to museums. The act ends the institution and begins three new fights.

- #poland_card_finish

@sld_ipn_archive
title: Separate the archive from the prosecutor
subtitle: End the institution's political concentration without closing every function at once.
