= Socialist, Not Social-Democratic

PPS's programme says the party represents a socialist, not a social-democratic,
worldview. Its delegates want the distinction recorded: managing capitalism
better is not the same aim as replacing the primacy of private profit.

- @pps_socialist_line
- @pps_socialist_federal
- @pps_socialist_refuse

@pps_socialist_line
title: Recognise a socialist current with its own programme
subtitle: PPS becomes a visible pole; economic clarity rises as party and coalition unity fray.
on-arrival: pps_strength += 5; pps_dissent -= 10; razem_strength += 2; labor_strength += 2; workers_support += 4; union_trust += 3; left_economic_position -= 4; capitalism_acceptance -= 6; party_unity -= 3; barons_dissent += 5; market_liberal_dissent += 7; ko_relation -= 5; news_headline = "Lewica recognises PPS as an explicitly socialist programme current"

The common platform now contains a disagreement about the final destination,
not only the next tax rate. Nobody can call the difference merely historical.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_socialist_federal
title: Give PPS a protected socialist caucus
subtitle: Preserve the distinction inside a plural common party without adopting it as the whole line.
