= Democracy Beyond Participatory Pennies

PPS calls participatory budgets too small to count as shared power. It wants
referenda, public hearings, citizens' initiatives and municipalities able to
intervene in laws and regulations that affect them.

- @pps_local_power
- @pps_local_initiative
- @pps_local_refuse

@pps_local_power
title: Write direct democracy and local initiative into the programme
subtitle: PPS and local organisers surge; central leadership and disciplined councils lose control.
on-arrival: pps_strength += 4; pps_dissent -= 8; local_network += 6; organiser_energy += 4; movement_autonomy += 5; public_trust += 4; institutional_trust += 3; leadership_authority -= 3; barons_dissent += 5; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "PPS demands local referenda, hearings and legislative initiative"

Residents receive routes to make, amend and block—not merely allocate a decorative
fraction. Party councillors discover that empowerment includes being overruled.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_local_initiative
title: Guarantee hearings and citizens' legislative initiatives
subtitle: Start with agenda power while leaving binding referenda for a later settlement.
on-arrival: pps_strength += 2; pps_dissent -= 5; local_network += 4; organiser_energy += 3; public_trust += 4; institutional_trust += 2; leadership_authority -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica guarantees public hearings and citizens' local initiatives"

The public gains the right to force an argument onto the agenda. Elected bodies
retain the last vote and acquire the burden of answering in daylight.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_local_refuse
