= Five Hundred Złoty at the First Bell

The new programme offers five hundred złoty to every family when a child enters
first grade. Parents know exactly what shoes, books and bags cost; fiscal staff
know that a memorable round number rapidly becomes an entitlement.

- @nowa_lewica_first_bell_universal
- @nowa_lewica_first_bell_progressive
- @nowa_lewica_first_bell_refuse

@nowa_lewica_first_bell_universal
title: Put the universal payment on every leaflet
subtitle: A promise no family must prove itself poor to receive; the programme bill rises visibly.
on-arrival: party_unity += 4; household_security += 4; young_support += 5; women_support += 3; workers_support += 3; rural_support += 2; budget_promises += 3; public_trust += 2; market_liberal_dissent += 4; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "Nowa Lewica promises every first-grader a five-hundred-złoty start"

The payment arrives automatically from the pupil register before September.
Universality removes the stigma, the application and the temptation to forget
families just above a threshold.

- #poland_card_finish

@nowa_lewica_first_bell_progressive
title: Double it for poor families and taper the rest
subtitle: Target more help at the sharpest bills, accepting forms and a less elegant promise.
